{
  "dom_id": "step-q330661",
  "name": "Question 7",
  "problem": "The data below is taken from the table of values of the cumulative distribution function $Φ(z)$ for the standard normal distribution. Given that $Z∼N(0,1),$ compute $P(Z<-0.38).$\n\n| $z$ | $\\,0.07\\,$ | $\\,0.08\\,$ | $\\,0.09\\,$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $\\,0.2\\,$ | $\\,0.6064\\,$ | $\\,0.6103\\,$ | $\\,0.6141\\,$ |\n| $\\,0.3\\,$ | $\\,0.6443\\,$ | $\\,0.6480\\,$ | $\\,0.6517\\,$ |\n| $\\,0.4\\,$ | $\\,0.6808\\,$ | $\\,0.6844\\,$ | $\\,0.6879\\,$ |\n\n$P(Z<-0.38)=$\n{{field-1}}",
  "worked_solution": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/differential/14259374/assets/8a6467813ccf982906fb5d1d8cd5c5c88b984c22a1e238715c65315a7772249c.png)\n\nFor a random variable $Z∼N(0,1),$ we have the following symmetry property for $a>0:$\n\n$$\nP(Z>a)=P(Z<-a)=Φ(-a)\n$$\n\nWe're given that $Z∼N(0,1),$ and we wish to compute $P(Z<-0.38).$ The required probability is represented by the area shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/differential/14259374/assets/ee2aebec9953a09dca6eab5c7e5434240885a383a6701638fffdaa9ee9cfeb40.png)\n\nBy symmetry, this equals the area corresponding to the probability $P(Z>0.38).$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/differential/14259374/assets/619fae52bde8b2da729095f733e1ea1411132fffe70cc23e252a83cbb2e7ff23.png)\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(Z<-0.38) & =P(Z>0.38) \\\\  & =1-P(Z<0.38) \\\\  & =1-Φ(0.38) \\\\  & =1-0.6480 \\\\  & =0.3520.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
